      "title": "Cloud",
      "content": "In simpler terms, the \"cloud\" doesn't refer to something floating in the sky. Instead, when you use cloud services, you're accessing remote servers, powerful mainframe computers housed in large data centers, through the internet. The cloud computing model gives you, the customer, greater flexibility and scalability compared to traditional on-premises infrastructure.\n\nCloud computing is pivotal in our everyday lives, whether that means to access a cloud application such as Google Gmail, stream a movie on Netflix or play a cloud-hosted video game. With cloud computing, you get the computing power or storage you need, without having to own or manage the physical hardware yourself.",
      "summary": "* The \"cloud\" refers to remote servers and powerful mainframe computers housed in large data centers, accessed through the internet.\n* Cloud computing provides greater flexibility and scalability compared to traditional on-premises infrastructure.\n* Cloud computing is used in everyday life for accessing cloud applications, streaming movies, and playing cloud-hosted video games.\n* Cloud computing allows users to access computing power or storage without having to own or manage the physical hardware themselves.",
